{title: Joy to the World}
{key: D}
{time: 2/4}

[D]Joy to the world! the Lord [A7]is [D]come;
Let [G]earth re[A]ceive her [D]King;
Let every heart prepare Him room,
And heaven and nature sing,
And [A7]heaven and nature sing,
And [D]heaven, and heaven and na[A7]ture [D]sing.

[D]Joy to the world! the Sav[A7]ior [D]reigns;
Let [G]men their [A]songs em[D]ploy;
While fields and floods, rocks, hills, and plains
Repeat the sounding joy,
Re[A7]peat the sounding joy,
Re[D]peat, repeat the sound[A7]ing [D]joy.

[D]No more let sins and sor[A7]rows [D]grow,
Nor [G]thorns in[A]fest the [D]ground;
He comes to make His blessings flow
Far as the curse is found,
Far [A7]as the curse is found,
Far [D]as, far as the curse [A7]is [D]found.

[D]He rules the world with truth [A7]and [D]grace,
And [G]makes the [A]nations [D]prove
The glories of His righteousness,
And wonders of His love,
And [A7]wonders of His love,
And [D]wonders, wonders of [A7]His [D]love.
